{"content":[{"c":["AZMAVETH (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Town near Anathoth. Forty-two men from the town returned from the Babylonian exile with Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.24","r":"Ezra.2.24","rawR":"Ezra.2.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.24","value":"Ezra.2.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:24"},"; “Beth-azmaveth,” ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.28","r":"Neh.7.28","rawR":"Neh.7.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.28","value":"Neh.7.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:28"},"). Later, Azmaveth supplied singers to help celebrate the dedication of the rebuilt wall of Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.29","r":"Neh.12.29","rawR":"Neh.12.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.29","value":"Neh.12.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:29"},"). It has been identified as Hizmeh, a site five miles (8 kilometers) north of Jerusalem."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AzmavethPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.24","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.24","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.24"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.7.28","rawQueryValue":"Neh.7.28","sourceRefExact":"Neh.7.28"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.29","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.29","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.29"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ad9bb21f37dac16295afaf820e6f65c63280970e8592c46e7fd92823cc371a26","sourceItemName":"AzmavethPlace","sourceItemOrder":655,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AzmavethPlace","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Azmaveth (Place)","title":"Azmaveth (Place)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}